          "unverified": true,
          "note": "Cache read is the one place the spec contradicts itself. Section 1's table prints 0.25; section 2's mechanics say read = 0.1x input, which Sonnet (2 -> 0.2), Opus (5 -> 0.5) and Haiku (1 -> 0.1) all obey, making 0.25 the single outlier in a column otherwise generated by the rule. We follow section 2 (1.00) because over-charging a cache read makes the app quote MORE than it charges, which is the safe direction for a number shown to a user before they commit. Nothing routes to Fable in any default role. Re-verify against Anthropic's page before this model is ever routed to."
